  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reducing the Expansion of the Agricultural Frontier in the Coniferous and Broadleaf Forests of the Chiquibul Mayan Mountains Landscape, by supporting a Guatemala-Belize bi-national cooperation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project will reduce agricultural encroachment on broadleaf forest ecosystems of the Maya Mountains Chiquibul in Guatemala by 1) identifying areas of greatest pressure on the landscape, 2) developing sustainable livelihood pilot projects in hotspot border communities, and 3) working with the Agency for Protected Areas to strengthen monitoring and enforcement actions under the Environmental Security Strategy for the area and 4) implementing a communications campaign directed at local communities via radio to discourage illegal and unsustainable forest use and wildlife extraction and trade activities. The project has a strong complimentary bi-national linkage to LAC 1517 in Belize.</narrative>
  </description>
